# FreeBSD Emulation Framework - Example Configurations

This directory contains example configuration files for the FreeBSD emulation
framework. Configurations are organized by security level, architecture, and
device configuration. Choose the configuration that best matches your use case.

## Security-Level Configurations

| File | Security Level | Use Case |
|------|---------------|----------|
| `emu-basic.conf` | Insecure | Local development, isolated testing |
| `emu-standard.conf` | Standard | Development servers, general use |
| `emu-high.conf` | High | Production servers, sensitive data |
| `emu-maximum.conf` | Maximum | Critical infrastructure, highest security |

## Architecture-Specific Configurations

| File | Architecture | Use Case |
|------|-------------|----------|
| `emu-amd64.conf` | x86-64/AMD64 | Standard 64-bit x86 emulation |
| `emu-i386.conf` | i386/IA-32 | Legacy 32-bit x86 systems |
| `emu-arm64.conf` | ARM64/AArch64 | 64-bit ARM systems |
| `emu-powerpc-g3.conf` | PowerPC G3 | Classic Mac OS X / Mac OS 9 emulation |
| `emu-powerpc64.conf` | PowerPC 64-bit | Modern PowerPC (G4/G5), servers |
| `emu-riscv64.conf` | RISC-V 64-bit | Open-source RISC architecture |

## AMD64/x86-64 Variant Configurations

| File | Variant | Video | Use Case |
|------|---------|-------|----------|
| `emu-amd64.conf` | Standard | virtio-gpu | General purpose, all devices |
| `emu-amd64-desktop.conf` | Desktop | virtio-gpu | Workstation, software development |
| `emu-amd64-server.conf` | Server | none | High-performance server workloads |
| `emu-amd64-gaming.conf` | Gaming | stdvga | PC gaming with GPU pass-through |
| `emu-amd64-multimedia.conf` | Multimedia | virtio-gpu | HTPC, Kodi/PLEX, media center |
| `emu-amd64-security-workstation.conf` | Security | none | High-security sensitive workloads |
| `emu-amd64-legacy-compat.conf` | Legacy | cirrus | Windows XP/7, legacy OS compatibility |
| `emu-amd64-laptop.conf` | Laptop | virtio-gpu | Portable workstations, mobility |
| `emu-amd64-minimal.conf` | Minimal | none | Resource-constrained environments |
| `emu-amd64-compilefarm.conf` | Compile Farm | none | Build servers, HPC workloads |
| `emu-amd64-headless.conf` | Headless | none | Background services, CI/CD pipelines |

### Video Device Options

| Setting | Description |
|---------|------------|
| `video_device=none` | Headless (serial console only) |
| `video_device=stdvga` | Standard VGA, BIOS boot support |
| `video_device=cirrus` | Cirrus Logic GD5446, legacy Windows |
| `video_device=virtio-gpu` | Modern VirtIO GPU, Linux/BSD guests |
| `video_device=vmware-svga` | VMware SVGA II, compatibility mode |

### Resolution Options

| Setting | Dimensions | Use Case |
|---------|------------|----------|
| `video_width=640` | 640x480 | Legacy, minimal |
| `video_width=800` | 800x600 | Basic desktop |
| `video_width=1024` | 1024x768 | Standard desktop |
| `video_width=1280` | 1280x800 | Widescreen laptop |
| `video_width=1920` | 1920x1080 | Full HD (1080p) |
| `video_width=1920` | 1920x1200 | Widescreen 16:10 |
| `video_width=2560` | 2560x1440 | Quad HD (1440p) |
| `video_width=3840` | 3840x2160 | Ultra HD (4K) |

## Device-Specific Configurations

| File | Devices | Use Case |
|------|---------|----------|
| `emu-network-only.conf` | Network only | Routers, firewalls, network services |
| `emu-storage-only.conf` | Storage only | File servers, databases, air-gapped |
| `emu-no-devices.conf` | No devices | Pure computation, HPC, compile farms |
| `emu-minimal.conf` | Minimal | Embedded, IoT, resource-constrained |
| `emu-full-devices.conf` | All devices | Desktop, legacy hardware, testing |

## Security Level Comparison

| Feature | Basic | Standard | High | Maximum |
|---------|-------|----------|------|---------|
| Securelevel | -1 | 1 | 3 | 3 |
| MAC Enforcement | Off | On | On | On |
| Veriexec Check | Off | Auto | On | On |
| Audit Logging | Off | On | On | On |
| Network Isolation | Off | Off | On | On |
| Swap Encryption | Off | Off | On | On |
| Memory Encryption | Off | Off | On | On |
| Huge Pages | Off | Auto | On | On |
| NUMA Awareness | Off | On | On | On |
| RCTL Limits | Off | On | On | On |
| Max Instances | 128 | 32 | 16 | 8 |
| Max Memory (MB) | 131072 | 65536 | 32768 | 16384 |

## Installation

1. Choose the configuration matching your security requirements:

   ```bash
   # For development (insecure)
   cp emu-basic.conf /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf

   # For production (high security)
   cp emu-high.conf /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
   ```

2. Review and adjust settings as needed for your environment.

3. Create required directories:

   ```bash
   mkdir -p /var/emu /var/cache/emu/images
   chmod 750 /var/emu /var/cache/emu/images
   ```

## Host System Requirements

### Basic Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- No special requirements

### Standard Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- MAC framework enabled in kernel
- Sufficient system resources (4GB+ RAM recommended)

### High Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- MAC framework enabled in kernel
- MAC veriexec module loaded
- At least 8GB RAM recommended
- Swap encryption requires memory encryption capable CPU (AES-NI)

### Maximum Configuration
- FreeBSD 14.0 or later
- MAC framework enabled in kernel
- MAC veriexec module loaded with fingerprints configured
- At least 16GB RAM recommended
- CPU affinity requires system with 4+ cores
- All memory encryption features require capable CPU

## Kernel Module Loading

Load the emulation framework kernel module:

```bash
# As root
kldload emu_core
```

To load at boot, add to `/etc/rc.conf`:

```
emu_load="YES"
```

## Verification

Verify the module is loaded:

```bash
kldstat | grep emu_core
```

Check sysctl settings:

```bash
sysctl kern.emulation
```

## Documentation

See the following man pages for more information:

- `emu(8)` - Emulation framework command reference
- `emu.conf(5)` - Configuration file format

## Troubleshooting

### Module fails to load
Check dmesg for errors:
```bash
dmesg | tail -50
```

### Permission denied errors
Ensure you have appropriate privileges or are running as root.

### Configuration not being read
Check that `/usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf` exists and is readable.
